- Expected results table (directional predictions, not fake numbers — careful: the researcher asked for a "tabla de resultados esperada (expected results table)" — this means a table of the expected/placeholder format, i.e., a template of what the results table should look like, along with the qualitative expectations). Provide a template table + qualitative expectations: CycleNet ≤ seasonal naive ≤ MA in S1–S3; ablation ≥ CycleNet (worse); all methods ≈ comparable in S4 (no degradation penalty > 10%); S5: CycleNet with learnable bank ≈ fixed bank at P=32, plain MLP worse.
- Statistical check: paired comparison of per-seed MAE (CycleNet vs ablation, vs seasonal naive): simple paired t-test or Wilcoxon hand-rolled; n=5 is small — report the sign of the differences and treat statistical claims cautiously.

