- S5: success if the learnable bank approaches the fixed-P model (within 10% MAE).

**(h) Feasibility and constraints**
- Compute: benchmark forward pass 1.4 ms/batch → epoch ≈ 9 batches × (forward+backward ≈ 3–4× forward) ≈ 40–55 ms → 300 epochs ≈ 15 seconds per fit. Total fits: 5 seeds × (5 series × 2 models (CycleNet + ablation)) = 50 fits ≈ 15–20 minutes CPU, plus baselines (trivial, seconds). Total budget: well under 1 hour on 1 core; parallelizable to minutes with 224 cores. Memory: negligible (<100 MB). Disk: logs/tables <10 MB.
- Limitations: no numpy/torch → hand-rolled linear algebra (vector ops, matrix products, OLS via Gaussian elimination); no plotting → save figures as SVG/ASCII, or just text tables (matplotlib not available; can hand-emit SVG polylines — optional); Python 3.14 stdlib random is deterministic; no pip install; /workspace has only 39 GB free — no problem.
- What can't be done: no public datasets, no GPU, no frameworks, no hyperparameter search beyond the few specified (grid search over L ∈ {48,96} only for the main series S1).
- Determinism and reproducibility: all seeds logged; scripts single-file stdlib.

**(i) Limitations of the design**
