- Known/limited periods; S5 only partially tests unknown periods (bank is discrete).
- Single horizon design h=12, fixed; no probabilistic/quantile forecasts (point forecasts only).
- Small model, no deep learning; results may not transfer to larger networks/datasets.
- White noise / random walk control is simple; real non-periodic series have autocorrelated noise (an AR(1) variant could be added — noted as an extension).
- Standardization with train-only statistics leaks nothing but assumes stationarity of scale (S4 random walk is non-stationary — noted).
- 5 seeds → limited statistical power; directional conclusions only.

